---
import DesignSystemShell from "../../layouts/DesignSystemShell.astro";
import DsSection from "../../components/design-system/DsSection.astro";
import DsRule from "../../components/design-system/DsRule.astro";
import DsSpec from "../../components/design-system/DsSpec.astro";
---

<DesignSystemShell slug="accessibility" source="deployment/remote/dashboard/Design.md § Accessibility · standards/design/v1.md DSN-005">
  <DsSection id="floor" title="The floor">
    <p>
      WCAG 2.2 Level AA is the floor for every surface, public or internal. It is not a compliance exercise: the same
      constraints that make a board usable with a screen reader — visible focus, status in words, labelled controls,
      real tables — are what make it usable at the end of a long Friday. Every text pairing is measured on the
      <a href="/design-system/color#contrast">colour chapter</a>; the rest of the criteria are below with how each is met.
    </p>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Criterion</th><th>Level</th><th>How the system meets it</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1.1.1 Non-text content</td><td>A</td><td>Alt-text rules per image kind (Icons & images → Alt text); decorative SVG is <code>aria-hidden</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1.3.1 Info and relationships</td><td>A</td><td>Real <code>table</code>, <code>th</code>, <code>details/summary</code>, <code>label for</code>; headings in outline order; groups have <code>role="group"</code> + <code>aria-label</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1.3.2 Meaningful sequence</td><td>A</td><td>Detail panels reorder after the list at ≤ 1180 in DOM order, not with CSS <code>order</code> alone (the invoice rail uses <code>order</code> — recorded exception to revisit).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1.4.1 Use of colour</td><td>A</td><td>Status is a word plus colour; rings have labels; charts have tables.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1.4.3 Contrast (minimum)</td><td>AA</td><td>4.5:1 text, 3:1 large text — measured in both modes.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1.4.4 Resize text</td><td>AA</td><td>Rem/px sizes with no max-scale; layout survives 200% zoom by scrolling inside wrappers.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1.4.10 Reflow</td><td>AA</td><td>Single column at ≤ 820; wide tables scroll themselves; 320px floor.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1.4.11 Non-text contrast</td><td>AA</td><td>Borders ≥ 3:1 against both adjacent surfaces (<code>#e5e7eb</code> on white is 1.2:1 — decorative separators only; control borders use <code>--border-strong</code> or the focus ring).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1.4.12 Text spacing</td><td>AA</td><td>No fixed-height text containers; rows grow.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1.4.13 Content on hover or focus</td><td>AA</td><td>Tooltips are native <code>title</code>; popouts close on Escape.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2.1.1 Keyboard</td><td>A</td><td>Every control is a <code>button</code>, <code>a</code>, <code>input</code> or <code>summary</code>; no click-only divs.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2.4.3 Focus order</td><td>A</td><td>DOM order = visual order; the one shared popout is inserted after its trigger row.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2.4.7 Focus visible</td><td>AA</td><td><strong>Known gap:</strong> the shell stylesheet has no <code>:focus-visible</code> rules today; browsers' default ring shows. Rule A-02 below makes the ring explicit; adopt it on every surface.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2.4.11 Focus not obscured</td><td>AA</td><td>Sticky headers and bottom bars use <code>scroll-margin</code> / <code>scroll-padding</code> so a focused row is never under them.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2.5.5 / 2.5.8 Target size</td><td>AAA / AA</td><td>44px in the shell and on mobile; 36px on desktop-only boards (meets 2.5.8's 24px minimum).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>3.2.2 On input</td><td>A</td><td>Changing a select filters; it never navigates or submits.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>3.3.1 / 3.3.3 Errors</td><td>A / AA</td><td>Inline saves flash red and keep the value; the note names what to fix.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>4.1.2 Name, role, value</td><td>A</td><td>Filter KPIs carry <code>aria-pressed</code>; toasts are <code>role="status"</code>; popouts <code>role="dialog"</code>; the theme trio is a labelled group.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>4.1.3 Status messages</td><td>AA</td><td>The single toast node is <code>aria-live="polite"</code>; save flashes are accompanied by a status message.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="focus" title="Focus & keyboard">
    <DsSpec label="Focus ring" code=":focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--primary); outline-offset: 2px } — gold in dark" layout="stack">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center">
        <button class="button button-ghost button-small" type="button" style="outline:2px solid var(--ds-focus);outline-offset:2px">Focused ghost</button>
        <button class="button button-primary button-small" type="button" style="outline:2px solid var(--ds-focus);outline-offset:2px">Focused primary</button>
        <input class="ds-search" style="max-width:200px;background:var(--surface);color:var(--text);border-color:var(--ds-focus)" value="Focused input (border moves)" readonly />
        <a href="#focus" style="outline:2px solid var(--ds-focus);outline-offset:2px;border-radius:2px">Focused link</a>
      </div>
      <small style="color:var(--text-muted)">Inputs move their border to the focus colour instead of adding a ring; everything else gets the 2px ring with 2px offset. Never <code>outline: none</code> without a replacement.</small>
    </DsSpec>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Where</th><th>Does</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><span class="ds-kbd">Tab</span> / <span class="ds-kbd">Shift</span>+<span class="ds-kbd">Tab</span></td><td>Everywhere</td><td>Moves through controls in DOM order; skips <code>aria-hidden</code> and hidden legacy inputs.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="ds-kbd">Enter</span> / <span class="ds-kbd">Space</span></td><td>Summary rows, KPI cards, segments</td><td>Toggles / activates; a summary with an input inside stops propagation so typing does not collapse it.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="ds-kbd">Esc</span></td><td>Popout, dropdown, search</td><td>Closes / clears; focus returns to the trigger.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="ds-kbd">←</span> <span class="ds-kbd">→</span></td><td>Segmented / scope control</td><td>Moves the active segment (roving tabindex).</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="ds-kbd">↑</span> <span class="ds-kbd">↓</span></td><td>Search results, select</td><td>Native behaviour.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="ds-kbd">⌘</span>/<span class="ds-kbd">Ctrl</span>+<span class="ds-kbd">S</span></td><td>—</td><td>Not bound; the browser keeps it. No global shortcuts that swallow browser keys.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="aria" title="ARIA patterns in use">
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Pattern</th><th>Markup</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Toggle filter</td><td><code>button[aria-pressed]</code></td><td>Board KPI pills, cash-map cells</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Grouped choice</td><td><code>div[role=group][aria-label] &gt; button.is-active</code></td><td>Theme trio, scope control</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Disclosure</td><td>native <code>details/summary</code>; chevron <code>aria-hidden</code></td><td>Rail departments, trees, More filters</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Current page</td><td><code>a[aria-current=page]</code></td><td>Rail links, chapter nav</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Non-navigating item</td><td><code>span[aria-disabled=true]</code> + badge</td><td>"soon" leaves</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Status message</td><td><code>[role=status][aria-live=polite]</code></td><td>Toast</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Popout</td><td><code>[role=dialog][aria-modal=false][aria-labelledby]</code></td><td>WIP best-guess popout</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Icon button</td><td><code>button[aria-label]</code> + <code>svg[aria-hidden]</code></td><td>Rail toggle</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Chart</td><td><code>canvas[role=img][aria-label]</code> + table</td><td>Executive pipeline</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Legend</td><td><code>ul[aria-label]</code></td><td>Runtime board, map legend</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Region</td><td><code>section[aria-label]</code>, <code>aside[aria-label]</code>, <code>nav[aria-label]</code></td><td>Shell landmarks</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Not used, on purpose: <code>role="table"</code> on divs (use a table), <code>tabindex &gt; 0</code>, <code>aria-live="assertive"</code>, custom select widgets (native <code>select</code> is the standard).</p>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="color-independence" title="Color independence">
    <DsSpec label="The same row in greyscale still reads" layout="block">
      <div style="display:grid;gap:8px;width:100%">
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap"><span class="health-badge health-ready">Ready</span><span class="health-badge health-watch">Watch</span><span class="health-badge health-blocked">Blocked</span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-muted)">← colour</span></div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;filter:grayscale(1)"><span class="health-badge health-ready">Ready</span><span class="health-badge health-watch">Watch</span><span class="health-badge health-blocked">Blocked</span><span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-muted)">← greyscale: the words carry it</span></div>
      </div>
    </DsSpec>
    <ul>
      <li>Every pill has a word. Every light has a word and a time. Every ring has a legend entry and an alt.</li>
      <li>Negative numbers carry a minus sign as well as red; overdue cells are bold as well as red.</li>
      <li>Chart series are named in a legend and on-bar labels; a chart with more than two series adds a pattern or direct labels.</li>
      <li>The one place colour alone was tolerated — the vendor-map marker ring — carries its meaning in the popup chips and the legend.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="forms" title="Forms & errors">
    <ul>
      <li>Every input has a visible <code>label</code> (or <code>aria-label</code> on a compact board field with a visible column header).</li>
      <li>Placeholder is a hint, never the label; it lists what search matches.</li>
      <li>Errors are inline, next to the field, in the error family, stating what to change; the field keeps the user's value.</li>
      <li>Required actions are not disabled without a reason; a disabled control keeps a tooltip that says why.</li>
      <li>Confirmations state the scope and the non-effects in plain sentences (Content → Messages).</li>
      <li>No time limits on forms; the vendor magic link's expiry is stated in the prompt.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="a11y-rules" title="Rules">
    <div class="ds-rules">
      <DsRule id="A-01" title="WCAG 2.2 AA on every surface, both modes; contrast is measured, not eyeballed." source="DSN-005; Color → Contrast matrix">
        <p>Use the matrix; add a pairing to it before using it.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="A-02" title="Focus is visible: 2px ring in the focus colour with 2px offset on every control; inputs move their border. Never outline: none without a replacement." source="Design.md Accessibility; recorded gap: no :focus-visible in global.css (2026-09-14)">
        <p>Adopt on the shell and every board; the design-system site already does.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="A-03" title="Status is never colour alone: word + colour, sign + colour, weight + colour." source="Design.md; docs/109 legend">
        <p>Greyscale test before ship.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="A-04" title="Native elements first: button, a, input, select, details, table. No click-only divs, no div tables, no custom selects." source="docs/40 §5; this chapter">
        <p>ARIA adds names and states to native elements; it never replaces them.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="A-05" title="Every image has alt per its kind; every chart has a label and a table; every icon-only control has an aria-label." source="Icons & images I-03; I-07">
        <p>"logo" and filenames are failures.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="A-06" title="Targets: 44px shell and mobile, 36px desktop boards, 8px between; nothing under 24px." source="Design.md 'Comfortable hit areas'; WCAG 2.5.8">
        <p>Pills are not targets; the row is.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="A-07" title="One live region per surface (the toast, polite); no assertive regions; no global shortcuts that swallow browser keys." source="invoice-audit.astro:194">
        <p>Escape closes; focus returns to the trigger.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="A-08" title="Reflow to one column at ≤ 820 with no horizontal page scroll; 200% zoom works; pinch-zoom is never disabled." source="Mobile M-05, M-06">
        <p>Wide things scroll themselves.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="A-09" title="Reduced motion is honoured on every animated surface." source="Motion MO-06">
        <p>The information survives without the motion.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="A-10" title="Ship gate: axe-core against the built page in both modes with zero violations; Lighthouse accessibility ≥ 95." source="Design.md 'Catch it automatically'; agent handbook">
        <p>The daily sweep cannot reach WorkOS-gated pages; run the check locally with a session.</p>
      </DsRule>
    </div>
  </DsSection>
</DesignSystemShell>
